Subject: [PATCH] R80b, part 6, patch 16 (cld-advisor, at main's word in M16;
 main's third folder, section 2, row A14): B1885'S VERDICT FILE SAYS THREE
 CHECKS IN ITS SCOPE AS IN ITS VERDICT LINE

A reader's check of main's answers at Review 80 (agy-002's; row A14, held by main). The verdict line of
B1885 was corrected to say that three checks are made on the grid at 18 digits, A4, A5 and H5. The scope of
the same file still said "the two checks made on it".

The scope says three, with their names, and a dated bracket keeps what it read. The lock holds the scope
and the verdict line to one count, and holds that the old words stand once, after their correction.

The second half of the row, main's plant against this lock that changed nothing, is patch 8 of this part:
made as main made it properly at the landing, the lock fails.

The lock passes: 8 tests. Every gate passes but the count of landings. The row is held by main.

BUILT AGAIN ON MAIN'S 663a902ff (2026-11-13): main corrected the scope itself at Review 81 (the SM seat's finding 09), by
a bracket after the words that said two. This patch now leaves the verdict file as main wrote it, and brings only the
lock: the scope is held to say three checks, A4, A5 and H5, after the words that said two.
---
 .../test_b1885_the_golden_state_on_the_whole_verified.py   | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/frontier/B1885_the_golden_state_on_the_whole_verified/verification/test_b1885_the_golden_state_on_the_whole_verified.py b/frontier/B1885_the_golden_state_on_the_whole_verified/verification/test_b1885_the_golden_state_on_the_whole_verified.py
index a20944c23..765d90390 100644
--- a/frontier/B1885_the_golden_state_on_the_whole_verified/verification/test_b1885_the_golden_state_on_the_whole_verified.py
+++ b/frontier/B1885_the_golden_state_on_the_whole_verified/verification/test_b1885_the_golden_state_on_the_whole_verified.py
@@ -142,6 +142,13 @@ def test_the_verdict_and_the_note_on_the_grids_precision_are_held():
     v = json.loads((ARC / "arc_verdict.json").read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
     assert v["verdict"] == "PROVED"
     assert "18 for the grid and the three checks made on it, A4, A5 and H5" in v["claim_one_line"]
+    # ADDED 2026-11-12 (Review 80; a reader's check of main's answers, its row A14, held by main): the scope of this same file
+    # still said "the two checks made on it".  The verdict line and the scope are held to one count.
+    scope = v["scope"]["hypotheses"]
+    # Built again on main's 663a902ff (2026-11-13): main corrected the scope itself at Review 81 (the SM seat's finding 09),
+    # by a bracket after the words that said two; the scope is held to say three checks, A4, A5 and H5, after them.
+    assert "the two checks made on it [CORRECTED 2026-11-13 (Review 81" in scope
+    assert "three checks, A4, A5 and H5" in scope and scope.index("the two checks made on it") < scope.index("three checks, A4, A5 and H5")
     f = (ARC / "FINDINGS.md").read_text(encoding="utf-8")
     assert "the grid is made at 18 digits, and three checks are made on it: A4, A5 and H5" in f
     # the three are the script's: the checks it makes on the grid's values, after the precision is put back to 30
